# Dashboard and Report UI Rules

Applies to `src/components/saq/`, `src/app/saq/dashboard/`, `src/app/saq/report/`, and shared SAQ chrome under `src/app/saq/layout.tsx`.

## Shared SAQ shell

- **`app/saq/layout.tsx`** wraps SAQ routes with **`SaqAuthenticatedHeader`** (nav: Home, Workspace), optional **`BetaBanner`**, and a **dark canvas** (`bg-slate-900`); content cards stay **light** for contrast.
- Page titles use **`GrissaPageHeader`** / **`GrissaPageTitleStrip`**. Subtitle tone defaults to **canvas**; use **`descriptionTone="onLight"`** inside white/print blocks only.
- Assessment / dashboard / report load data for the active **`versionId`** (see `useAssessmentVersionRoute`); do not invent a second version-resolution path in these pages.

## Dashboard

- Keep hierarchy clear: at-a-glance metrics, capability/priority summaries, theme and action distribution.
- Use engine outputs as source data (same as assessment flow / report).
- Action plan effort is shown as S/M/L and means the size of the work. When to act (Immediate / Urgent / Planned) is the calculated timing and is labeled that way on the action plan, dashboard, and report. Assignee is a collaborator name or a typed team name, stored in the existing leader field. The note field is labeled Next step and is not filled from the recommended action.
- The Workspace standards list has Category and Industry filters. Evidence rows show Current level and Target level. Checklist lines for one level sit under a single “To achieve level N:” heading and are numbered.
- **`DashboardInfoBanner`**, **`DashboardSection`** (`headingSurface="canvas"` by default), **`ReadinessHeroCard`** — flat white card + semantic accent.
- Users without edit access: read-only UX; defer access rules to `permissions.ts` + repository.

## Report and PDF

- **`ReportInfoBanner`** (`print:hidden`); keep browser-print/PDF coherent with **`ReportPurposeNote`** when used.
- PDF via `AssessmentReportPDF` (`@react-pdf/renderer`) from engine-derived data — not DOM screenshot (`html2canvas`/`jspdf` are not the export path).
- Preserve stakeholder hierarchy: purpose/methodology, interpretation, summaries, action planning.
- Avoid duplicating toolbar metadata inside the report body.

## Editing Guidance

- Reuse existing report primitives (`ReportSection`, summary/action cards, interpretation blocks).
- Maintain print-safe spacing, typography, and page-break behavior.
- For cross-layer boundaries, defer to `architecture.mdc`.
